19021:
Matching elastic properties and moduli from NCERT Physics (Mechanical Properties of Solids):
Young's Modulus (Y): Ratio of longitudinal stress to longitudinal strain:
Y = \frac{F / A}{\Delta L / L} = \frac{FL}{A(\Delta L)} \longrightarrow \textbf{A-II}

Compressibility (K): Reciprocal of bulk modulus:
K = \frac{1}{B} = -\frac{1}{\Delta P}\left(\frac{\Delta V}{V}\right) \longrightarrow \textbf{B-III}

Bulk Modulus (B): Ratio of hydraulic stress to volumetric strain:
B = -\frac{\Delta P}{\Delta V / V} = -P\left(\frac{V}{\Delta V}\right) \longrightarrow \textbf{C-IV}

Poisson's Ratio (\sigma): Ratio of lateral strain to longitudinal strain:
\sigma = \frac{\Delta d / d}{\Delta L / L} = \frac{\Delta d}{\Delta L}\left(\frac{L}{d}\right) \longrightarrow \textbf{D-I}

Matching sequence: A-II, B-III, C-IV, D-I.
→ (D)

19023:
