Height: h = 20\text{ m}
Time taken: t = 10\text{ s}
Acceleration due to gravity: g = 9.8\text{ m/s}^2

W = 1000 \times 9.8 \times 20 = 196,000\text{ J}

Calculate power delivered by the crane:
P = \frac{W}{t} = \frac{196,000\text{ J}}{10\text{ s}} = 19,600\text{ W} = 19.6\text{ kW}
→ (C)

19044:
Calculate the value of 1 Vernier Scale Division (VSD):
Given that 20\text{ VSD} = 16\text{ MSD}:
1\text{ VSD} = \frac{16}{20}\text{ MSD} = \frac{4}{5}\text{ MSD} = 0.8\text{ MSD}

Given 1\text{ MSD} = 1\text{ mm}:
1\text{ VSD} = 0.8 \times 1\text{ mm} = 0.8\text{ mm}

Calculate Least Count (LC) of the vernier callipers:
LC = 1\text{ MSD} - 1\text{ VSD} = 1\text{ mm} - 0.8\text{ mm} = 0.2\text{ mm}

Convert to centimeters:
LC = \frac{0.2\text{ mm}}{10} = 0.02\text{ cm}
→ (C)

19045:
The distance s fallen by a freely falling body released from rest during reaction time t is:
s = \frac{1}{2} g t^2

Since g is constant, the distance travelled is directly proportional to the square of reaction time (s \propto t^2):
A larger reaction time results in a strictly greater distance fallen.

Compare the given reaction times:
Person B: t_B = 0.22\text{ s}
Person E: t_E = 0.21\text{ s}
Person A: t_A = 0.20\text{ s}
Person D: t_D = 0.19\text{ s}
Person C: t_C = 0.18\text{ s}

Arranging in descending order of reaction times:
t_B > t_E > t_A > t_D > t_C

Therefore, the distances travelled by the ruler follow:
B > E > A > D > C
→ (C)

19048:
Magnetic field at the centre of a circular coil of N turns and radius r:
B = \frac{\mu_0 N I}{2 r}

Given:
N = 100
r = 5\text{ cm} = 0.05\text{ m}
B = 3.14 \times 10^{-3}\text{ T} = \pi \times 10^{-3}\text{ T}
\mu_0 = 4\pi \times 10^{-7}\text{ T m/A}

\pi \times 10^{-3} = \frac{(4\pi \times 10^{-7}) \times 100 \times I}{2 \times 0.05}
\pi \times 10^{-3} = \frac{4\pi \times 10^{-5} \times I}{0.1} = 4\pi \times 10^{-4} \times I
I = \frac{\pi \times 10^{-3}}{4\pi \times 10^{-4}} = \frac{10}{4} = 2.5\text{ A}

Calculate magnetic moment (M) of the coil:
M = N I A = N I (\pi r^2)
M = 100 \times 2.5 \times \pi \times (0.05)^2 = 250 \times 3.1416 \times 0.0025 \approx 1.963\text{ A m}^2 \approx 2\text{ A m}^2

Thus, current is 2.5\text{ A} and magnetic moment is 2\text{ A m}^2.
→ (D)

